<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Page-1" id="jPIsLkbbkSyFe4eVlREV">
    <mxGraphModel dx="3357" dy="1215" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Hello Interview Delivery Framework&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Requirement Gathering (Functional &amp;amp; Non-functional)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Entity extraction &amp;amp; API design&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. Data flow (for backend data oriented heavy questions)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. Basic HLD that satisfies functional requirements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5. Deep dives into non-functional requirements&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="179" width="518" x="-22" y="117" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Functional requirements&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="179" x="-216" y="395" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="1. User is able to see Top K viewed videos from all time&amp;nbsp;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="332" x="-241" y="477" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="2. User is able to see Top-K viewed videos in last month/week/day/hour etc" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="419" x="-235" y="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-5" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Concept of tumbling and sliding windows" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="288" x="-276" y="634" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-6" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Tumbling windows: fixed windows always, example: last week always means from Monday to Sunday&amp;nbsp;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="454" x="-252.5" y="703" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-7" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Sliding windows: variable windows always, example: last week can mean data from today (Tuesday) till last Tuesday" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="522" x="-272" y="795" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-8" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="In the context of our problem, we&#39;ll go for tumbling windows: week (7 days), month (28 days) etc&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;for the sake of ease&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="537" x="-272" y="887" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-9" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Out of scope functional requirement:" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="280" x="-298.5" y="972" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-10" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="* Arbitrary time window (eg: give me top K videos as it existed on 19th Jan)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="437" x="-277" y="1019" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-11" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Non-functional requirements&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="228" x="809" y="389" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-12" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="A. 1 minute between when the event happens and when it is tabulated in&amp;nbsp; our top K&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Reasoning:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. In distributed systems, due to network congestion, failure modes, retry etc, there is always a chance of getting data delay upto 1 min, out of order data etc&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Setting an expectation of 1 minute delay also gives us the leeway to serve data from cache which might be stale upto 1 min&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="142" width="454" x="717" y="454" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-13" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="B. Low latency on the read path (retrieving top K videos): tens of milliseconds are acceptable&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;This also gives an hint that we would require caching since read latency in this range is possible only with cache&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="544" x="680" y="667" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-14" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="C. Scale of the system:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;• Billions of Youtube videos (TBD)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;• Hundreds of thousand of videos per second (TBD)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The idea of scale gives a hint that sorting on read path will not work and we have to go for pre-computation of top K&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="124" width="544" x="663" y="778" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-16" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="D. Precise results are required (no approximations)&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;It is often times easier to design for systems that support precise&amp;nbsp; results than building good approximations&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="376" x="691" y="989" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-17" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Entities &amp;amp; API design" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="137" x="-292" y="1236" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-18" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Entities&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Video&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;View&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;TimeWindow&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="-288" y="1338" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-20" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="API&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;GET /views/top-k?window={window}&amp;amp;k={k}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Returns: Array of {videoId, views} sorted in descending order of views&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="102" width="415" x="201.5" y="1299" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-21" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Notes:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. window in this context means &#39;last week&#39;, &#39;last month&#39; etc.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. k is assumed to be small enough in this problem (max 1000). Hence, pagination is not required&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="118" width="236" x="216" y="1469" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-22" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="HLD that satisfies basic functional requirements" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="359" x="-813" y="1714" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-23" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Note that in the context of my problem, the focus is on top K.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Hence, I can assume that the data of views in present in a Kafka topic, which is already available and can be consumed.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="81" width="383" x="-801" y="1782" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-24" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Video Views (Kafka topic)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="173" x="-773" y="2265" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-25" edge="1" parent="1" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-600" y="2297" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="-488.85" y="2297" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-26" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="View Consumer" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="63" width="173" x="-483" y="2265" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-27" edge="1" parent="1" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-310" y="2297" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="-219.51" y="2297" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-28" parent="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;aspect=fixed;" value="Views DB&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;(Postgres)&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="102" width="102" x="-217" y="2245.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-29" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="VideoViews&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;• videoId&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;• views&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;• timestamp&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Index on timestamp is created for fast range queries&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="118" width="204" x="60" y="2250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-30" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Note:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Timestamp in above schema doesn&#39;t mean exact timestamp at which the view occurred, but the hourly time bucket (9-10 PM, 10-11 PM etc) in which the view landed&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="69" width="233" x="60" y="2435" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-31" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Top K Fetch Service" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="-469" y="2113" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-32" edge="1" parent="1" source="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-31" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-28" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="67" y="2419" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="117" y="2369" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-33" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="API Gateway" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="63" width="120" x="-768" y="2113" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-35" edge="1" parent="1" source="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-33" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-31" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="67" y="2419" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="117" y="2369" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-36" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="SQL query for fetching top K:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;SELECT videoId, SUM(views) as views&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;FROM videoViews&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;WHERE timstamp &amp;gt;= {windowStart} AND timestamp &amp;lt;= {windowEnd}&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;GROUP BY videoId&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;ORDER BY SUM(views) DESC LIMIT {k}&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="94" width="391" x="-899" y="2514" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-38" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Note: this basic HLD satisfies all functional requirements, but it is not scalable, low latency etc&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;We will cover these non-functional requirements in the next sections&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="403" x="-920" y="2762" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-39" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Deep dives into non-functional requirements" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="239" x="-1001" y="2925" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-41" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="A. Low latency (tens of milliseconds) on the read path" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="368" x="-1047" y="3004" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2RgB2zIPSqEstAvz9yk-42" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Right now, the Database query is being hit on the read path everytime, which results in higher latency.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;A better solution would to be have a cron job running at hourly cadence (since the minimum granularity at which we support top K views is hourly). This cron job will fetch the top K video views from each individual shard, compute the global top K and then store it in Redis Cache.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Any client who fetches the top K will always read off the Redis cache&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Failure mode discussion:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;If the cron job fails to compute at hourly cadence, what are the different possible options?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;A. In case of cache miss, start querying the DB to fetch the top K.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;But, this is a terrible idea, since the million of read queries will start hammering DB, and it can make the system fail badly.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;B. Fallback to the last known top-K from previous computation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Example: if the cron job run at 10 AM failed, then return data from previous run at 9 AM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Note: this will introduce staleness in data, but it is the best possible failure mode remediation that doesn&#39;t make the system fail badly.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="242" width="548" x="-1028" y="3172" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
